# 2. Git Branching Strategy

## 2.1 Strategy Model

`batmanoverlay` utilizes a **Trunk-Based Development** model with short-lived feature branches and strict Pull Request (PR) validation.

```
main (protected) ───────────●──────────────────●─────────────●──────── (v1.0.0)
                             \                /             /
feature/clp-fts               └───●───────●──┘             /
                                   (PR #12)               /
fix/hotkey-conflict                                └─●──●┘
                                                      (PR #15)
```

## 2.2 Branch Naming Conventions

All branch names MUST follow the format: `<type>/<issue-id>-<short-description>`

| Type | Purpose | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `feature/` | New functional capability | `feature/42-clipboard-fts` |
| `fix/` | Bug fix | `fix/88-hotkey-conflict` |
| `chore/` | Maintenance, dependencies, tooling | `chore/101-update-deps` |
| `docs/` | Documentation changes | `docs/15-readme-update` |
| `perf/` | Performance optimization | `perf/63-fts-query-speed` |
| `refactor/` | Code refactoring without behavioral changes | `refactor/31-json-store` |

## 2.3 Commit Message Standard (Conventional Commits)

Commit messages MUST strictly follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

### Allowed Types

- `feat`: A new feature (maps to minor version bump)
- `fix`: A bug fix (maps to patch version bump)
- `docs`: Documentation only changes
- `style`: Formatting, missing semi colons, etc. (no code change)
- `refactor`: Refactoring production code
- `perf`: Code change that improves performance
- `test`: Adding or correcting tests
- `chore`: Updating build tasks, package manager configs, etc.

### Allowed Scopes

`core`, `browser`, `clipboard`, `typing`, `ui`, `storage`, `platform`, `models`, `deps`, `ci`

### Commit Message Examples

```git
feat(clipboard): implement FTS5 search ranking in ClipboardStore

Closes #42
```

```git
fix(typing): prevent worker thread deadlock on target window loss

Fixes #88
```

## 2.4 Branch Protection Rules on `main`

- **Require a pull request before merging**
  - Require at least 1 approving review from Code Owners
  - Dismiss stale pull request approvals when new commits are pushed
- **Require status checks to pass before merging**
  - `CI / Lint & Type Check (ruff, mypy)`
  - `CI / Unit Tests (pytest)`
  - `CI / Architecture Boundaries (import-linter)`
  - `CI / Security Audit (pip-audit)`
- **Require branch to be up to date before merging**
- **Require linear history** (Squash and merge or Rebase and merge)
- **Do not allow bypassing the above settings**

