# 13. Release Strategy

## 13.1 Versioning

Version numbers follow **Semantic Versioning 2.0.0** (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`):
- `MAJOR`: Incompatible architectural changes.
- `MINOR`: New features added in a backward-compatible manner.
- `PATCH`: Backward-compatible bug fixes.

## 13.2 Automated Release Workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`)

```yaml
name: Release

on:
  push:
    tags:
      - 'v*'

jobs:
  build-release:
    name: Build Portable Release Package
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Set up Python 3.11
        uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: '3.11'

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: |
          python -m pip install --upgrade pip
          pip install -r requirements-dev.txt

      - name: Run Build Script
        run: python scripts/build.py

      - name: Compress Release Archive
        shell: powershell
        run: |
          Compress-Archive -Path dist/batmanoverlay -DestinationPath dist/batmanoverlay-${{ github.ref_name }}-windows-x64.zip

      - name: Generate SHA-256 Checksum
        shell: powershell
        run: |
          Get-FileHash -Path dist/batmanoverlay-${{ github.ref_name }}-windows-x64.zip -Algorithm SHA256 | Format-List > dist/checksums.txt

      - name: Create GitHub Release
        uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v2
        with:
          files: |
            dist/batmanoverlay-${{ github.ref_name }}-windows-x64.zip
            dist/checksums.txt
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
```

